  "title": "linx: Use add_item_ret_length instead of an extra tvb_strnlen",
  "description": "If adding a FT_STRINGZ, it is more efficient to use the _ret_length\nfunction than to retrieve the length a second time when the tree is\nvisible. Also, the existing code was incorrect because it failed to\nadvance past the terminating NULL, as tvb_strnlen (but not tvb_strsize)\ndoes not include the '\\0' terminator, though in the sample capture\nfiles those strings were at the end.",
